  "note": "市集西头、市集东头、铁盾会门前 (native:fanfang/bazaar_west, bazaar_east, bazaar_north; 番坊 A): the bazaar's one street of beaten yellow earth, crowded — west the glass stall with its beads catching the sun under a red-and-gold awning, carpets hung on poles and stacked, the old storyteller on his felt with his copper bowl; the 市舶司's grey compound wall on the south side with its board; east the spice sacks open-mouthed under an ochre-and-violet awning, the coppersmith's rack of kettles and plates, a hostel for the merchants; the black-stone 拜火祠 squat across the street's east end, smoke curling from its roof where the fire has burned three hundred years; north up a short lane 铁盾会's heavy gate with the two great shields either side. The houses mixed: flat-roofed mud-brick ones the 胡商 built, tiled ones the port's own; striped cloth over the doors. Old and used: spice dust and straw in the ruts, a broken cart, water jars, washing on lines.",
